[size=5][b]Display & UI Tweaks[/b][/size]

Play No Rest for the Wicked on any screen shape: ultrawide, 16:10, square, tall, and the Steam Deck. The mod unlocks every resolution, adds UI area and UI size settings to the game's own Options menu, a drag-and-drop HUD layout editor, and an option to hide the HUD outside combat.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Every resolution your display supports can be picked in Options > Display. The game hides anything narrower than 16:10 or wider than 32:9, and replaces such a saved resolution at every launch.
[*]No black 16:9 bars around the world on non-16:9 screens.
[*]The whole UI (HUD, menus, dialogue) is kept in a UI area of any shape, set with one slider.
[*]Menus shrink to fit the UI area instead of being cut off.
[*]Everything stays inside the UI area, also the parts the game pins to the screen edges: the bounty and challenge boards, the map's detail bar, bounties on the HUD, item pickups, the hint bar, the boss bar, the plague meter and the area banner.
[/list]

New rows at the bottom of [b]Options > Display[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]UI Area[/b] (1.00-4.00, default 1.78): the shape of the area the whole UI is kept in, width divided by height. 1.00 = square, 1.78 = 16:9, 2.33 = 21:9, 3.56 = 32:9. Replaces the game's UI Aspect Mode.
[*][b]HUD & Dialogue UI Size[/b] (10-150%): in-game HUD, overlays and dialogue.
[*][b]Menu UI Size[/b] (10-150%): inventory, stats, map, settings and the other menus.
[*][b]Edit HUD Layout[/b]: drag, resize and reset HUD elements on top of the game, with sample content in empty elements (chat, item pickups, bounties, teammates, boss bar). Works from the main menu too.
[*][b]Reset HUD Layout[/b]: every HUD element back where the game has it.
[*][b]Hide HUD Outside Combat[/b] (Off / On / On, but show health while hurt): fades out health, equipment, money, durability, clock and location a few seconds after combat. Item pickups, hints and chat stay.
[/list]
With the defaults on a 16:9 monitor the game looks exactly as before. On wider monitors the UI area starts at 16:9: raise UI Area to use more of the screen width.

[size=4][b]Examples[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ultrawide:[/b] keep UI Area at 1.78 for a 16:9 UI in the middle of the screen, or raise it (2.33 for 21:9) to spread the UI out.
[*][b]Square or tall monitor:[/b] pick your resolution, set UI Area to 1.00, then adjust HUD & Dialogue UI Size to taste.
[*][b]Steam Deck:[/b] works as is; use the size sliders if the text is too small.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader/releases]MelonLoader[/url] 0.7.3 or newer.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install MelonLoader into the game folder and start the game once.
[*]Extract the mod's zip into the game folder, so that [i]DisplayUiTweaks.dll[/i] ends up in the [i]Mods[/i] folder.
[/list]

[b]Steam Deck / Linux (Proton):[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Copy the files from MelonLoader's [i]MelonLoader.x64.zip[/i] (the Windows build) into the game folder, and the mod into [i]Mods[/i].
[*]In Steam, open the game's Properties > General > Launch Options and enter: [code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="version=n,b" %command%[/code]
[*]Start the game. On the first start MelonLoader installs the .NET runtime it needs by itself; that start takes a minute or two.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tested with game build 29466 and MelonLoader 0.7.3 on Windows and on a Steam Deck.
[*]Display only: nothing in the game simulation or your save is changed, so it does not affect co-op.
[*]All settings are also in [i]UserData/MelonPreferences.cfg[/i], section [DisplayUiTweaks], including a switch for each feature.
[/list]

